  [1m[36mNote Update (1.6ms)[0m  [1m[33mUPDATE "notes" SET "content" = 'Project Lumyo – Feature Planning & Architecture Review
Date: May 7, 2026
Participants: Vlad, Alex, Marina, Radu

Overview
The goal of this meeting was to align on the next major milestone for Lumyo: the public beta launch. We reviewed the current state of the RAG pipeline, discussed outstanding UX issues, and outlined the roadmap for the next six weeks. There''s growing excitement around the knowledge graph features, but also some concern about latency in the retrieval layer.

RAG Pipeline Status
The hybrid retrieval system is mostly functional. Pinecone is handling dense vector search well, and the BM25 sparse layer is improving recall for exact-match queries. The main bottleneck right now is the Cohere Rerank step — it adds roughly 400–600ms of latency on complex queries with graph-expanded chunks. Radu suggested we experiment with caching rerank results for frequently accessed note clusters.
Neo4j AuraDB is stable. The graph traversal logic correctly expands from seed chunks to related notes via LINKS_TO and MENTIONS relationships. One open issue: notes with fewer than three outgoing edges tend to get under-represented in retrieval results, even when they''re semantically highly relevant. We need a fallback weighting strategy for isolated nodes.
Chunking is working as designed — markdown-aware, 300–600 token windows with a metadata prefix per chunk. However, Marina flagged that code blocks inside notes are sometimes split mid-block, which breaks syntax context. This needs a fix before beta.

UX & Product
The editor feels solid. Inline AI suggestions are fast and contextually relevant for most note types. The main complaint from internal testers is that the sidebar knowledge graph visualization is too cluttered for users with more than 200 notes. We''ll need to implement a filtered view — possibly scoped to the last 30 days of activity or to a user-defined tag set.
Search UX needs work. The current results page doesn''t distinguish between graph-expanded results and direct semantic matches, which confuses users. Alex proposed a visual indicator — a small graph icon next to graph-expanded results — so users understand why certain notes appear.
Mobile is out of scope for beta but Vlad mentioned that the API layer should be designed with mobile clients in 
mind from day one.', "updated_at" = '2026-05-07 08:46:19.223315' WHERE "notes"."id" = 3 /*action='update',application='LumioServer',controller='notes'*/[0m
